READ ME for folder "scenarios"
Author: Rebecca Chisholm, La Trobe University, 2026

This folder contains files to run all of the scenarios for figures 3-5 in the 
manuscript and the corresponding supplementary sensitivity analyses.

===============================================================================
1. RUN MODEL SCENARIOS
===============================================================================

First, run:
    Simulate_all_scenarios.R

This script uses the functions defined in:
    Single_scenario.R

and saves the simulated trajectories as RData files in the folder:
    output/


PRIMARY SCENARIO ANALYSES

The primary scenario analyses consider combinations of:
    - Baseline endemic mf prevalence:
        approximately 30%, 50%, and 70%
    - Drug:
        ivermectin or moxidectin
    - MDA frequency:
        annual or biannual
    - Model:
        variable-response (VR) or GR-only

The VR simulations use parameter combinations retained under the primary
calibration.

CALIBRATION SENSITIVITY ANALYSES

Additional scenario simulations are performed to assess whether the main
scenario results are sensitive to assumptions made during model calibration.

These analyses are restricted to:
    - approximately 70% baseline endemic mf prevalence
    - ivermectin MDA
    - annual and biannual MDA
    - VR and GR-only models

Results are generated for the primary calibration and four sensitivity
analyses:
    1. Moderate SOR increase:
       SOR worm proportion increases by 0.05-0.10 during the calibration
       period.
    2. Weak SOR increase:
       SOR worm proportion increases by 0-0.05 during the calibration period.
    3. No offspring-phenotype selection:
       s_SOR,SOR = s_SOR,GR = 0.
    4. Wider prevalence calibration:
       final mf prevalence of 8-14%, compared with 10-12% in the primary
       calibration.

For the GR-only scenarios, the y values from the corresponding retained VR
calibration parameter combinations are used.

===============================================================================
2. PROCESS MODEL OUTPUTS
===============================================================================

Next, run:
    process_all_scenario_outputs.R

This script loads the scenario RData files generated above and calculates
summary outcomes for each retained parameter combination.

These include:
    - initial SOR worm proportion
    - final SOR worm proportion
    - final mf prevalence
    - phenotype-specific mf prevalence
    - time to reach pOTTIS

The initial SOR worm proportion is evaluated at time zero, immediately before
the effect of the first MDA round.

If a trajectory does not reach pOTTIS during the simulated programme, its
time to pOTTIS is recorded as NA.

The script combines all available scenarios into a single long-format data
frame:
    processed_all

and saves:
    processed_all_scenarios.RData
    processed_all_scenarios.csv

The RData file also contains:
    scenario_manifest

which records the model, drug, treatment frequency, calibration analysis,
baseline transmission setting, and source file associated with each scenario.

===============================================================================
3. CREATE FIGURES
===============================================================================

Next, run:
    create_figures_revised.R

This script loads:
    processed_all_scenarios.RData

and generates versions of the primary scenario figures comparing
outcomes across the three baseline endemic prevalence settings.

It also generates figures comparing results across the primary calibration
and all four calibration sensitivity analyses at approximately 70% baseline
prevalence.

Figures are saved in:
    figures/

===============================================================================
4. CREATE TABLES
===============================================================================

Next, run:
    create_tables_revised.R

This script loads:
    processed_all_scenarios.RData

and generates summary tables for the scenario analyses.

For the primary analyses, tables summarise results across the three baseline
endemic prevalence settings.

For the sensitivity analyses, comparative tables summarise the primary and
four sensitivity calibrations at approximately 70% baseline prevalence.

Summary statistics include the median and 2.5th-97.5th percentiles.

For time to pOTTIS, the sensitivity tables additionally report the number and
proportion of trajectories that reach pOTTIS, so trajectories that do not
reach the threshold are explicitly represented.

Tables are saved in:
    tables/

===============================================================================
ADDITIONAL SCRIPTS
===============================================================================

Single_scenario.R
    Contains the functions used by Simulate_all_scenarios.R to simulate the
    VR and GR-only models for a specified parameter set, baseline transmission
    setting, drug, and MDA frequency.

run_once.R
    Runs a single realisation of the model for a specified parameterisation
    and produces plots of the resulting trajectory.

===============================================================================
ORDER IN WHICH TO RUN THE MAIN SCRIPTS
===============================================================================

    1. Simulate_all_scenarios.R
    2. process_all_scenario_outputs.R
    3. create_figures_revised.R
    4. create_tables_revised.R